<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Boer War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1880">1880</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Transvaal War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> War was a revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> Boers against the British annexation of their republic in 1877. Beginning in December 1880, Boer commandos besieged British garrisons and defeated British columns at Laing's Nek and, decisively, at Majuba Hill on 27 February 1881. Gladstone's government then made peace, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria-convention">Pretoria Convention</a> of 1881 restored self-government to the South African Republic under British suzerainty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-boer-war.jpg" alt="First Boer War" width="320" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fidodog14 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_Boer_War_Collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
